1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,227
Asterfield Family Pickup turns a household request into one confirmed pharmacy pickup.

2
00:00:05,227 --> 00:00:10,454
This is the working local product, using fictional people and pharmacy records,

3
00:00:10,454 --> 00:00:15,680
simulated payments, and a real local AI interpreter.

4
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:22,444
The family organizer already has approved access to four saved routines. Prescription

5
00:00:22,444 --> 00:00:28,204
items use existing refill records and confirmed demonstration prices. The agent does

6
00:00:28,204 --> 00:00:33,964
not select treatments or change prescriptions.

7
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:40,250
Before ordering, Alex explicitly allows these saved items, up to fifty dollars

8
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:45,530
per order. That permission has a separate total allowance, order limit and

9
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:50,810
expiry. A spoken request cannot grant itself extra authority.

10
00:00:51,811 --> 00:00:55,811
First, a request with a thirty five dollar limit. The full family

11
00:00:55,811 --> 00:00:59,811
basket costs forty dollars and ninety eight cents. The system stops. It

12
00:00:59,811 --> 00:01:03,811
does not remove somebody's item or use the larger standing allowance to

13
00:01:03,811 --> 00:01:07,811
ignore the request.

14
00:01:08,814 --> 00:01:13,267
Now Alex speaks the request. This recorded voice goes through the browser

15
00:01:13,267 --> 00:01:17,720
microphone pipeline and the real local speech recognizer, then into the AI

16
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:22,174
workflow.

17
00:01:22,598 --> 00:01:30,598
Alex: Order the regular medicines for my dad, mom, sister and myself from the nearest pharmacy to home. You can pay up to $50.

18
00:01:55,768 --> 00:02:10,888
Assistant: Your family order is accepted at Asterfield Cedar Square, 208 Cedar Avenue, Asterfield. The total is 40 dollars and 98 cents. The pharmacy will let you know when it is ready for pickup.

19
00:02:12,064 --> 00:02:16,944
The backend checks family access, refill eligibility, stock and budget. Cedar Square

20
00:02:16,944 --> 00:02:21,824
is selected because the closer store cannot fill the complete basket. Payment

21
00:02:21,824 --> 00:02:26,704
is authorized. The order is accepted, but it is not ready and

22
00:02:26,704 --> 00:02:31,584
has not yet been charged.

23
00:02:32,589 --> 00:02:37,789
The pharmacy team sees the same order in its own facility queue.

24
00:02:37,789 --> 00:02:42,989
A staff member reviews eligibility and prepares every saved item. Only after

25
00:02:42,989 --> 00:02:48,189
that confirmation does the backend capture payment and mark the pickup ready.

26
00:02:49,189 --> 00:02:53,189
Back in Alex's account, the ready message and pickup code come from

27
00:02:53,189 --> 00:02:57,189
the recorded order status. The complete basket, pickup address and confirmed payment

28
00:02:57,189 --> 00:03:01,189
are visible together.

29
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:16,000
Assistant: Your family order is ready for pickup at Cedar Square. Payment of 40 dollars and 98 cents is confirmed.

30
00:03:17,647 --> 00:03:22,847
At the pharmacy desk, the customer supplies the pickup code. The handover

31
00:03:22,847 --> 00:03:28,047
is confirmed through the fulfillment service. Repeated commands resolve to the same

32
00:03:28,047 --> 00:03:33,247
order rather than creating another purchase.

33
00:03:34,249 --> 00:03:39,829
The customer history now shows a completed pickup. One request, four family

34
00:03:39,829 --> 00:03:45,409
members, one location, and a verified outcome. This browser product is a

35
00:03:45,409 --> 00:03:50,989
standalone foundation for a future in car interface. It is not a

36
00:03:50,989 --> 00:03:56,569
native CarPlay application or a live pharmacy integration.
